{title: Raise a Hallelujah}
{subtitle: Ich rufe Halleluja}
{song_number: 114}
{language: en}
{tempo: 82}
{time: 4/4}
{key: D}
{composer: Jonathan David Helser, Melissa Helser, Molly Skaggs, Jake Stevens}
{lyricist: Jonathan David Helser, Melissa Helser, Molly Skaggs, Jake Stevens}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D]I raise a hallelujah in the [G]presence of my enemies.
[Bm7]I raise a hallelujah, [Asus4]louder than the unbelief.
[D]I raise a hallelujah, my [G]weapon is a melody.
[Bm7]I raise a hallelujah, [A]Heaven comes to fight for me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[D]I raise a hallelujah with [G]everything inside of me.
[Bm7]I raise a hallelujah; [Asus4]I will watch the darkness flee.
[D]I raise a hallelujah in the [G]middle of the mystery.
[Bm7]I raise a hallelujah; [A]fear, you lost your hold on me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]I'm gonna sing in the [D]middle of the storm.
[Bm7]Louder and louder, you're gonna [A]hear my praises roar.
[G]Up from the ashes, [D]hope will arise.
[Bm7]Death is defeated; the [A]King is alive.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: 1}
[D]Sing a little louder (sing a little louder).
[Asus4]Sing a little louder (sing a little louder).
[Bm7]Sing a little louder (sing a little louder).
[G]Sing a little louder (sing a little louder).
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_bridge: 2}
[D]Sing a little louder in the presence of my enemies.
[Asus4]Sing a little louder, louder than the unbelief.
[Bm7]Sing a little louder, my weapon is a melody.
[G]Sing a little louder, Heaven comes to fight for me.
[G]Sing a little louder.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Coda}
[D]I raise a hallelujah.
[G]I raise a hallelujah.
[Bm7]I raise a hallelujah.
[Asus4]I raise a hallelujah[G].
{end_of_chorus}
{comment: Source order: verse 1, chorus, verse 2, chorus, bridge 1, bridge 2, chorus, coda.}
